problemStatement:
## Improve Touch Targets

You are given a mobile bottom navigation bar. The buttons are currently 24px by 24px with no spacing, making them hard to tap. Fix the CSS so that each tappable area is at least 44x44 CSS pixels, and there is at least 8px gap between buttons. The visual icon can remain 24x24, but the interactive area must be larger.

```html
<nav class="mobile-nav">
  <ul>
    <li><a href="#home"><span class="icon">🏠</span> Home</a></li>
    <li><a href="#search"><span class="icon">🔍</span> Search</a></li>
    <li><a href="#profile"><span class="icon">👤</span> Profile</a></li>
  </ul>
</nav>
```

```css
.mobile-nav ul {
  display: flex;
  list-style: none;
  padding: 0;
  margin: 0;
}
.mobile-nav a {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  text-decoration: none;
  color: #333;
  font-size: 12px;
}
.icon {
  font-size: 24px;
}
```

Modify the CSS to ensure each link has a minimum tappable area of 44x44px and add gap between items. Keep the visual appearance similar.

solutionCode:
.mobile-nav ul {
  display: flex;
  list-style: none;
  padding: 0;
  margin: 0;
  gap: 8px;
}
.mobile-nav a {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  text-decoration: none;
  color: #333;
  font-size: 12px;
  padding: 10px; /* expands tap area while icon remains visually small */
  min-width: 44px;
  min-height: 44px;
  box-sizing: border-box;
}
.icon {
  font-size: 24px;
}
